>>>markdown
# US Flights: Which Carriers Fly Where?

This notebook explores a sample of US domestic flights. The data is a public Parquet file
hosted on GitHub, and every query below runs **in your browser** with DuckDB.

Edit any cell and press **Shift+Enter** to re-run it.
>>>markdown
## The model

First we define a source. It joins each flight to its carrier and its origin airport, and
adds a few reusable measures.
>>>malloy
source: carriers is duckdb.table('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/malloydata/malloy-samples/main/data/carriers.parquet') extend {
  primary_key: code
}

source: airports is duckdb.table('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/malloydata/malloy-samples/main/data/airports.parquet') extend {
  primary_key: code
  measure: airport_count is count()
}

source: flights is duckdb.table('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/malloydata/malloy-samples/main/data/flights.parquet') extend {
  join_one: carriers with carrier
  join_one: origin_airport is airports with origin
  join_one: dest_airport is airports with destination

  measure:
    flight_count is count()
    total_distance is distance.sum()
    avg_delay is round(avg(arr_delay), 1)
    pct_late is round(count() { where: arr_delay > 15 } / count() * 100, 1)
}
>>>markdown
## Busiest carriers
>>>malloy
# bar_chart
run: flights -> {
  group_by: carriers.nickname
  aggregate: flight_count
  order_by: flight_count desc
  limit: 10
}
>>>markdown
## Flights per month

Malloy truncates timestamps with `.month`, and the renderer draws a line chart.
>>>malloy
# line_chart
run: flights -> {
  group_by: flight_month is dep_time.month
  aggregate: flight_count
  order_by: flight_month
}
>>>markdown
## Nested results

One of Malloy's strengths is nesting. For each of the top five carriers, here are its
busiest origin airports and how often it is late.
>>>malloy
run: flights -> {
  group_by: carriers.nickname
  aggregate: flight_count, avg_delay, pct_late
  limit: 5
  nest: top_origins is {
    group_by: origin_airport.city, origin_airport.state
    aggregate: flight_count
    limit: 4
  }
}
>>>markdown
## Airports by state

A plain table from the airports file.
>>>malloy
run: airports -> {
  group_by: state
  aggregate: airport_count
  order_by: airport_count desc
  limit: 8
}
